WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.780
- [Narrator] It's one of the most iconic

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.960
hairstyles of all time: bangs.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.670
Also known as fringe.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.070
But we'll get to that later.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.390
Bangs have been immortalized
by countless movie stars

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.090
and cultural icons.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.420
So, where did bangs come from?

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.900
How does one cut them?

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.320
And what does having bangs say
about the women bold enough

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.330
to wear them?

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.323
This is how bangs took over the world.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.163
Bangs date all the way
back to the 8th century.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.470
People often credit the
Egyptian queen Cleopatra

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.940
for bringing them into style.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.173
But that's just a myth.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.880
Historians say the credit
should go to this guy.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.550
His name was Zuriab,

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.400
an Iraqi Renaissance man known
to have started the trend.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.240
Which, as this painting shows,

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.903
was also adopted by his female fans.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.190
Over the next thousand years,
bangs became an institution

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:11.203
evident in countless
paintings of European women

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:14.023
in the 18th and 19th centuries.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.880
With the dawn of motion pictures,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.210
silent film stars like Louise Brooks

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.683
made bangs an iconic style
of the Roaring Twenties.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.620
Then came the era of the pinup girl.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.503
Pioneered by the notorious Betty Page.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.360
Europe moved back into the
spotlight in the swinging 60s

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.700
with iconic looks by model Peggy Moffitt

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.260
and singer Jane Birkin.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.980
Only in Europe, they
don't call them bangs.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.460
They call it fringe.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.150
Which is what the style is
known as pretty much everywhere

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.231
except the US.

00:01:51.231 --> 00:01:53.279
So fringe continued to evolve.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.913
And sometimes the results were mixed.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.930
But the look has endured and
some of the most iconic women

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.230
in the world have made
sure that bangs, or fringe,

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.600
whatever you want to call it
is one of the most sought after

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.190
styles on the planet.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.570
And those brave enough to get them

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.320
usually come with inspiration.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.770
- I love Taylor Swift's bangs.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:12.603
- Taylor Swift

00:02:12.603 --> 00:02:13.770
- Taylor Swift.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:14.603
- Emma Stone.

00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:15.720
- Reese Witherspoon.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.610
- Alexa Chung.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.010
- Natalia Dyer.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.230
- Zooey Deschanel.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.990
- Zooey Deschanel has some great bangs.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.277
- [Narrator] So, how does
one actually get bangs?

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.548
Well, that depends on the type
of bangs you're going for.

00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:31.020
There's blunt, wispy,
shaggy, choppy, curly,

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.973
side swept, the options are endless.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.660
We went to Prema hair, in the
Lower East Side of Manhattan

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.413
to see how it's done for
both straight and curly hair.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.440
- When someone with straight
hair comes in for a fringe,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.730
generally we'll want to blow
dry all of the hair forward

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.540
to make sure that we don't
have any partings in there.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.080
Draw the hair to the center,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.333
go ahead and cut and then soften
that line in through there.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.980
When someone has curly hair,

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.150
because the hair doesn't
quite sit the same way,

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.180
I like to go through and
cut each curl individually

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.070
to make sure that it's
A, following the line

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:16.020
in through there but also shows
movement as the curls move.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.500
- [Narrator] But you don't
have to go to a salon

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.823
to get fabulous bangs.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.793
Lots of women prefer to do it themselves.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:30.693
Carefully.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:40.411
- Bangs.

00:03:40.411 --> 00:03:41.310
(laughs)

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.492
- [Narrator] So why do women get bangs?

00:03:43.492 --> 00:03:45.600
Well, let's ask them.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.730
- My bangs are 100% a part of my identity.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.740
- I just kind of wanted
this whole new look

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.700
for a new chapter.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.370
- Sometimes I just like to switch it up.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.690
- It's kind of cliche but
I actually went to Paris

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.330
and a lot of girls had them
and they just looked so good.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.060
- I like the way that they frame my face.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.240
I feel like I like myself with them more.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.838
- I grew them out once
and I absolutely hated it

00:04:05.838 --> 00:04:07.370
(laughs) and never did it again.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.880
- It was the first time my
haircut really felt like me

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.523
because it wasn't my mom
picking my hairstyle.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.720
- For the first couple of days

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.440
it might want to live like this.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.320
After a week or so, that
fringe will start to settle in

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.899
to it's new position and make
your life a whole lot easier.

00:04:21.899 --> 00:04:23.780
- [Narrator] Bangs may look effortless

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.280
but maintaining them is anything but.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.570
- Bangs are super high-maintenance.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.790
It's easy to put them in your
hair but once they're there,

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.100
it's a commitment for sure.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.100
- I straighten them every
day with a straightener.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.900
- The day's just split up
between pulling out the comb

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.510
and brushing them back down.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.570
- When it's really windy out
and the wind's hitting you

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.800
in both directions, and then it goes up.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.860
And then you're like, no, that's
not how I look, I promise.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:48.400
- [Narrator] In fact, they
can be so high-maintenance

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.210
they make some women
swear off fringe forever.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.930
- I actually am trying to
grow out my bangs right now.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.150
- The one reason why I hated them

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.390
was because it was just like
an extra step in the morning.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.364
- I had bangs as a baby because in the 90s

00:04:59.364 --> 00:05:01.430
that's just normal.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.820
Do you see this?

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.030
Look how cute I was.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.190
I don't know what happened.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:08.470
- People usually ask me, oh
why, I loved when you had bangs.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.380
I'm like, you loved me with
bangs but you wouldn't love

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.700
having them yourself, that's
pretty much what it is.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.186
It's just too much work.

00:05:15.186 --> 00:05:17.020
- [Narrator] But there are shortcuts.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.589
Like these clip in bangs
which don't require the months

00:05:18.589 --> 00:05:21.403
it takes to grow them back out.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.560
Bangs have been around for centuries,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.330
representing some of the most iconic

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.816
style moments of all time.

00:05:30.816 --> 00:05:34.419
They may be a lot of work but
one thing is pretty certain,

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:36.193
they're never going out of style.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.210
- I don't know, my face
was way too round for them.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.450
And then after awhile I'd wear
them on the side like that.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.930
Like, you can't really see that.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.822
But like, they wouldn't
fully cover my head.

00:05:51.822 --> 00:05:55.460
And another thing, is when
you're growing them out, like,

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.760
some of these pictures I have,

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.108
this is a picture of me ... whoops.

